            <ArticleTitle>The effects of nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory analgesics on pain after periodontal surgery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>731-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The results of this study indicate that nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory analgesics are effective for the control of periodontal postsurgical pain. In addition, these drugs are especially useful as they are nonaddictive and produce minimal CNS and gastrointestinal side effects.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
